WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:02.573
Bank of Canada independence.

00:00:02.523 --> 00:00:05.102
When your Prime Minister ran the bank.

00:00:05.102 --> 00:00:10.034
The Bank of Canada is supposed to operate independently from political interference.

00:00:10.034 --> 00:00:15.011
Its mandate is price stability — maintaining inflation near the two percent target.

00:00:15.011 --> 00:00:23.931
The Governor is appointed by the Board of Directors with the approval of Cabinet, serves a seven-year term, and is supposed to set monetary policy without political direction.

00:00:23.931 --> 00:00:33.386
But the current Prime Minister was Governor of the Bank of Canada from 2008 to 2013, then Governor of the Bank of England from 2013 to 2020.

00:00:33.386 --> 00:00:39.556
He is the only person in modern history to have run two major central banks and then become head of government.

00:00:39.556 --> 00:00:43.761
The question is not whether the Bank of Canada is formally independent.

00:00:43.761 --> 00:00:56.545
It is whether independence is meaningful when the PM who sets fiscal policy has deeper expertise in monetary policy than the Governor he effectively appointed, and when the PM's professional network spans the entire global central banking ecosystem.

00:00:56.545 --> 00:01:01.977
Three documented tensions between central bank independence and a PM from central banking.

00:01:01.977 --> 00:01:06.306
Documented impacts of monetary policy on Canadian families.

00:01:06.306 --> 00:01:09.386
The monetary layer of institutional capture.

00:01:09.386 --> 00:01:12.488
The Bank of Canada is formally independent.

00:01:12.488 --> 00:01:21.590
But formal independence within a captured institutional ecosystem means that monetary policy serves the same interests documented across every TENET5 investigation.

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:30.488
Quantitative easing inflated asset prices, benefiting the same pension funds, REITs, and institutional investors that profit from housing financialization.

00:01:30.488 --> 00:01:34.659
Rate hikes punished the mortgage holders who borrowed during the QE era.

00:01:34.659 --> 00:01:41.374
The fiscal-monetary coordination ensures that government spending creates the conditions that monetary policy must respond to.

00:01:41.374 --> 00:01:47.954
And the PM who sets fiscal policy has deeper central banking expertise than the Governor who sets monetary policy.

00:01:47.954 --> 00:01:52.113
The question is not whether the Bank of Canada is independent on paper.

00:01:52.113 --> 00:01:57.636
The question is whether independence is meaningful within the system architecture documented on this site.
